From 3157b58dcc5099457baf5720d77875717ed06a68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 17:55:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] i18n: seed the AutoScan and Mesh Nodes strings into all 25
 dictionaries

Groundwork for the two page commits that follow, landed first so their token
references resolve on any language.

RWIF_82 explains what the wireless sweep actually does: that each radio is swept
at the width it will run, that a router with two 5 GHz or two 6 GHz radios is
handled per radio, why DFS is skipped, and that a completed sweep leaves that
radio on a fixed channel. RWIF_31 and RWIF_33 are reworded to match.

RFWU_32..39 are the Mesh Nodes card on the firmware page.

English seed across all 25 files, so a non-English UI shows English rather than a
raw token until translated.
